       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is positive infinity (negative infinity), positive infinity (nega‐
       tive infinity) is returned.

       If _x is +0 (-0), +0 (-0) is returned.

       If the result overflows, a range error occurs, and the functions return
       HHUUGGEE__VVAALL, HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF, or HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively, with a sign  the  same
       as _x.

